cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Ischaemic stroke lesion segmentation on T1-weighted MRI: STRATIF-AI-BRE submission to the ISLES'26 challenge"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Amine
    family-names: Sadikine
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-4313-0476"
    affiliation: "CHRU de Brest, Brest, France"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-10-22
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/asadikine/isles26-stratif-ai-bre"
abstract: >-
  Source code and container of the algorithm submitted by team
  STRATIF-AI-BRE (published on Grand Challenge as "BRE SEG") to the ISLES'26 challenge, held at the SWITCH+ workshop of MICCAI 2026
  (27 September 2026). It segments
  ischaemic stroke lesions on skull-stripped T1-weighted brain MRI at acute,
  sub-acute and chronic stages, using an ensemble of three nnU-Net v2 folds.
  Research software, not a medical device. Developed within the STRATIF-AI
  project, funded by the European Union under Horizon Europe (grant
  agreement No 101080875).
keywords:
  - stroke
  - ischaemic stroke lesion segmentation
  - T1-weighted MRI
  - nnU-Net
  - ISLES'26
  - MICCAI 2026
  - SWITCH+ workshop
  - medical image segmentation
  - deep learning
